# Cross-tool collaboration

- Before changing files, inspect `git status --short`, relevant `git diff`, and `docs/COLLABORATION.md`.
- Treat existing modifications as owned by another tool or the user unless the task explicitly includes them.
- Discuss and obtain confirmation before changing experimental design, data splits, masks, models, metrics, baselines, training rules, or material compute budget.
- Record material adopted/rejected/frozen decisions and conflicts in `docs/COLLABORATION.md`; use `CHANGELOG.md` only for completed file facts.
- If code, protocol, changelog, or concurrent modifications disagree, record a verification item and stop short of choosing a version silently.
